---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Community | The Common Squamish" description="Learn how The Common brings people and local groups together in Squamish through coworking, gatherings, and community support.">
  <header class="page-hd"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow on-dark">Community at The Common</span><h1>Work together.<br />Grow together.</h1><p>The people who work here have always been part of the point.</p></div></header>
  <section class="section light"><div class="wrap split"><div><span class="kicker">Where the idea came from</span><h2>A desk is only the start.</h2><p>The Common took inspiration from Seats2meet in Utrecht and its idea of social capital. When people share what they know, make introductions, or give a little time, the whole space becomes more useful.</p><p>That's the thinking behind lunches, member socials, and the support The Common has offered to groups in Squamish.</p><a class="inline-link" href="https://www.seats2meet.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">About Seats2meet</a></div><img class="photo" src="/img/approved/shared-table.jpg" alt="Coworkers sharing a table at The Common" loading="lazy" /></div></section>
  <section class="section warm"><div class="wrap community-grid"><article><span class="kicker">At The Common</span><h2>Lunches and socials.</h2><p>Members have gathered over lunch and at informal socials. The kitchen and communal tables make it easy to talk with someone you might otherwise never meet.</p></article><article><span class="kicker">For Squamish</span><h2>Local groups and events.</h2><p>The Common has made room for community groups, entrepreneurs, and nonprofit gatherings. If you're planning something, tell us about it and we'll discuss what might work.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/contact/">Contact us</a></article></div></section>
  <section class="section light"><div class="wrap"><div class="program-intro"><span class="kicker">Past community programs</span><h2>Ways The Common has helped.</h2><p>These programs have been part of The Common's history. Please ask us which opportunities are available now.</p></div><div class="program-grid"><article><h3>Common Capital</h3><p>People contributed time, skills, or connections in exchange for more accessible desk space.</p></article><article><h3>Community grants</h3><p>Support for local groups working on entrepreneurship and innovation in Squamish.</p></article><article><h3>Venue sponsorship</h3><p>Support for community and nonprofit groups that needed a place to meet.</p></article></div><p class="program-link">Have an idea for the space? <a class="inline-link" href="/contact/">Tell us about it</a></p></div></section>
  <section class="section warm"><div class="wrap history"><span class="kicker">From our early years</span><h2>A few stories that shaped The Common.</h2><div class="history-grid"><article><span>2017</span><h3>Making room for community</h3><p>In an early note to members, Peter wrote openly about the work of turning a new coworking space into a real community. Member socials and conversations were part of that effort from the start.</p></article><article><span>2018</span><h3>Bringing Squamish together</h3><p>The Common hosted an all-candidates air hockey tournament in the 2018 local election season, with proceeds supporting Howe Sound Women’s Shelter. It was a playful example of the space acting as a local gathering place.</p></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="section light"><div class="wrap split"><img class="photo" src="/img/approved/courtyard.jpg" alt="The Common outdoor courtyard" loading="lazy" /><div><span class="kicker">Come in</span><h2>See the space for yourself.</h2><p>Book a desk for an hour or a day. If you like working here, you can ask us about a monthly plan.</p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/day-pass/">Book a desk</a></div></div></section>
</Base>
<style>.split h2,.community-grid h2,.program-intro h2,.history h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,3.5vw,3.2rem);letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:.8rem 0 1rem}.split p,.community-grid p,.program-intro p,.program-grid p,.history p{font-size:1.07rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:1.2rem}.community-grid,.history-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:clamp(2rem,5vw,5rem)}.community-grid article,.history-grid article{border-top:2px solid var(--forest);padding-top:1.5rem}.history-grid{margin-top:2rem}.history-grid span{color:var(--accent);font-weight:700}.history-grid h3{font-size:1.35rem;margin:.4rem 0}.program-intro{max-width:780px;margin-bottom:2rem}.program-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1.2rem}.program-grid article{border:1px solid var(--line);background:#fff;padding:1.6rem}.program-grid h3{font-size:1.35rem}.program-link{margin:1.5rem 0 0}@media(max-width:700px){.community-grid,.history-grid,.program-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style>
